experiment.prespecified:
Fixed 2026-11-19, before any result of this definition was read (borg-reborn-rs#556, PR #632; replaces
borg-zoo#364, which pinned the replaced design). Pilot (RULES 16); small and medium (starts 1-360, borg-zoo#240's
tier) only after this gate and the owner: breeder deaths are rare and 18 starts show direction only.
Gate:
- no config_error; one binary; each arm's two values in borg.txt and in params-core.json of the death replays;
- every cell ends in death, turn_cap or borg_stopped; frozen-turn bursts classified and key outliers listed;
- death bundles reproduced;
- in ctl, no "# Breeders cannot be stopped" and no "# Fighting through the breeders" note.
Report per arm and per class, from every game's messages:
- deaths and causes, final and maximum level, deepest level; breeder deaths (the killer has MULTIPLY);
- paired rescued and newly killed against ctl;
- breeder kills per game ("You have slain" a MULTIPLY race); "# Breeders cannot be stopped" per game, with its
  births and turns-a-kill;
- the breeder flees per game ("Fleeing (breeder level)", "Ignoring breeders (no recall)", scary-level flees with
  breeders known), and for stop-avoid "# Fighting through the breeders to the stairs";
- deaths within 500 game turns of a "# Breeders cannot be stopped" note.
Context: a local run on the same tree (18 classes-18 starts, 100,000 turns; not a zoo run): ctl 1 death, stop 3,
stop-avoid 2; sum of max CL 101 / 88 / 92 with a median paired change of 0; breeder kills 106 / 99 / 134.
